  "result": "Perfect! All 113 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## VAT Calculation \u2014 Implementation Complete \u2705\n\n### Key Features:\n\n**1. VAT Calculation Logic** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- `lineVat()` function calculates VAT per line on the amount **after discount**\n- Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n- Each line's VAT is **rounded individually** using `roundCents()`, then summed\n- Invoice VAT = sum of line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n\n**2. invoiceTotals Enhanced** \n- Now returns: `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- Calculation: `total = subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n- Order of operations: discount first, then VAT on the reduced amount\n\n**3. renderInvoiceText Updated**\n- Shows breakdown when there are discounts or VAT:\n  - **Subtotal** line (if discount > 0 or VAT > 0)\n  - **Discount** line (if discount > 0)\n  - **VAT** line (if VAT > 0)\n  - **Total** line (always shown)\n\n**4. VAT Rates Supported**\n- 21% (standard)\n- 9% (reduced)\n- 0% (zero-rated)\n\n### Example Calculation:\n\n| Component | Amount |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Line total (2 \u00d7 \u20ac85) | \u20ac170.00 |\n| Discount (10%) | -\u20ac17.00 |\n| **Amount after discount** | **\u20ac153.00** |\n| VAT (21% on \u20ac153) | \u20ac32.13 |\n| **Total** | **\u20ac185.13** |\n\n### Tests Added (17 new tests):\n\n- lineVat with 21%, 9%, 0% rates\n- VAT calculation on amount after discount\n- VAT rounding per line\n- Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n- invoiceTotals with discount and VAT\n- Tier discount combined with VAT\n- Rendering with VAT display\n\n**Total: 113 tests pass** (96 existing + 17 new VAT tests)",
